      "concept_ko": "그을려 늘어진 러시아 삼색기가 배경을 덮고, 중앙 오브젝트는 지평선까지 이어진 주유 대기 차량 행렬 하나. 대본 파트 2의 「기름 넣겠다고 늘어선 줄이 오 킬로미터 / 서른여섯 시간을 기다린 운전자」가 근거이며, 산유국이 기름을 못 넣는 자멸 국면이라 부정형으로 판정했다.",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the scene fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge as a single full-bleed image — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — that is the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — is the same continuous scene rendered dark, smoky and free of detail so overlay text stays readable, while all faces, flags, vehicles and key objects sit entirely within the upper five-eighths. Anything held or carried sits at mid height, never near the bottom edge. Heavy digital oil painting worked over a photographic base, thick visible brushwork and impasto texture on flags, smoke and metal, dramatic hard lighting, heavy atmospheric haze, one dominant colour drowning the frame, every part of the upper five-eighths packed edge to edge with elements and no empty space, cinematic wide-angle, very high contrast, painterly and rough rather than clean — a matte-painting finish, NOT a crisp photo composite, NOT a studio cut-out. An enormous Russian tricolour — horizontal white, blue and red bands — hangs across the whole width of the background as real heavy cloth, its edges charred black and soot staining the deep folds, the colours desaturated and grimy, raking orange firelight sweeping across it from the left. The single central object is a queue of fuel-starved cars and trucks that runs from the foreground into the vanishing point under a smoke-choked sky, engines dead, doors open, plastic cans standing on the roofs. In the right third, waist-up and standing directly in front of the flag, a Russian fuel-station attendant in a filthy hi-vis vest holds a dead nozzle down at his side because that is what he was doing when the pumps stopped. Brow furrowed deep, eyes cast down and unfocused at the concrete, lips pressed into a hard line, shoulders sunk. Firelight from the horizon puts a red key light on his face so it stays bright. no text, no letters, no words, no numbers, no captions, no watermark"
