      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the scene fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge as a single full-bleed image — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — that is the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — is the same continuous scene rendered dark, smoky and free of detail so overlay text stays readable, while all faces, flags and key objects sit entirely within the upper five-eighths. Anything held or carried sits at mid height, never near the bottom edge. Heavy digital oil painting worked over a photographic base, thick visible brushwork and impasto texture on flags, smoke and wood, dramatic hard lighting, heavy atmospheric haze, one dominant colour drowning the frame, every part of the upper five-eighths packed edge to edge with elements and no empty space, cinematic wide-angle, very high contrast, painterly and rough rather than clean — a matte-painting finish, NOT a crisp photo composite, NOT a studio cut-out. An enormous North Korean flag — a broad red band with a white circle bearing a red five-pointed star, thin white and blue stripes above and below — hangs across the entire background as heavy cloth, hard side light throwing its deep folds into shadow, the red gone dull and stained, its lower edge scorched but the star still fully readable. The single central object is a long row of plain wooden repatriation cases set out on frozen ground at mid height, running away into brown haze, each with a folded cloth on it. Behind them a thin file of soldiers stands at attention, smaller and hazier with distance. In the right third, waist-up in front of the flag, a North Korean woman in a padded coat and headscarf stands among the mourners with both hands hanging at her sides. Inner eyebrows lifted, eyes fixed on the nearest case without blinking, lower lip drawn in, chin trembling, shoulders pulled up. Cold orange light from a brazier off frame keeps her face bright against the dark. no text, no letters, no words, no numbers, no captions, no watermark"
