      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the scene fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge as a single full-bleed image — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — that is the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — is the same continuous scene rendered dark, smoky and free of detail so overlay text stays readable, while all faces, flags, packs and key objects sit entirely within the upper five-eighths. Anything held or carried sits at mid height, never near the bottom edge. Heavy digital oil painting worked over a photographic base, thick visible brushwork and impasto texture on flags, smoke and rusted steel, dramatic hard lighting, heavy atmospheric haze, one dominant colour drowning the frame, every part of the upper five-eighths packed edge to edge with elements and no empty space, cinematic wide-angle, very high contrast, painterly and rough rather than clean — a matte-painting finish, NOT a crisp photo composite, NOT a studio cut-out. Ground eye level, straight down the deck of a steel border bridge so the column walks out toward the camera between the girders. The left two-thirds is the disaster: an enormous North Korean flag — broad red band, white circle with a red five-pointed star, thin white and blue stripes above and below — hangs across the background as heavy cloth with its edges charred and soot in the folds, and beyond it a freight yard burns, a goods wagon lying on its side in the flame. In front of it a file of North Korean soldiers with heavy packs walks out toward the camera as if the fire behind them were nothing, the nearest one waist-up and sharp, the rest smaller and hazier down the bridge. The right third is divided off by a girder and a curtain of smoke: there, chest-up and standing in front of the flag, Kim Jong Un (leader of North Korea) is seen slightly from above, never from below, no hands in frame. Eyes narrowed almost shut and turned toward the column, one mouth corner drawn back in a tight satisfied line, chin dropped. Red firelight keeps his face bright while the bridge falls into smoke. no text, no letters, no words, no numbers, no captions, no watermark"
