      "purpose": "reference-inherit",
      "direction": "혼합",
      "concept_ko": "[모순] 뒤에서는 전선이 불타 무너지는데 그 앞으로 사람들이 멀쩡히 걸어 나온다 — 그리고 그들이 배워 온 것도 같이 나온다 / [남김] 좌 2/3 사건 대 우 1/3 인물 / 지상 눈높이 정면 / 우측 가슴 위 반신 / [바꿈] 피사체(북한군 대열 → 귀환하는 북한 장교 대열) / 인물(해설자 → 우리 쪽 한국 해군 장교) / 색온도(주황 화염 지배 → 좌측 화염 대 우측 차가운 여명). 혼합 판정 — 좌측 러·북은 부정형(그을린 국기), 우측 한국은 긍정형 처리로 태극기를 온전·선명하게 두고 열세는 그늘과 거리로만 만든다. 대본 파트 6의 「설계도는 복사가 되지만 경험은 사람에게 붙는다 / 그 땅 밑이 우리 서해고 동해다」가 근거.",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the scene fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge as a single full-bleed image — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — that is the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — is the same continuous scene rendered dark, smoky and free of detail so overlay text stays readable, while all faces, flags and key objects sit entirely within the upper five-eighths. Anything held or carried sits at mid height, never near the bottom edge. Heavy digital oil painting worked over a photographic base, thick visible brushwork and impasto texture on flags, smoke and water, dramatic hard lighting, heavy atmospheric haze, one dominant colour drowning the frame, every part of the upper five-eighths packed edge to edge with elements and no empty space, cinematic wide-angle, very high contrast, painterly and rough rather than clean — a matte-painting finish, NOT a crisp photo composite, NOT a studio cut-out. Ground eye level, straight down a shattered road so the column walks out toward the camera. The left two-thirds burns: an enormous Russian tricolour of white, blue and red bands and a North Korean flag with its white circle and red five-pointed star hang side by side across the background as heavy cloth, both charred at the edges and stained with soot, both still readable, a column of flame standing between them; a ruined front-line village smoulders behind. Out of that a file of North Korean officers walks toward the camera with map cases and radios, unhurried, the nearest one waist-up and sharp, the rest hazing out — what they learned walks out with them. The right third is a colder world divided off by smoke and grey dawn light: there, chest-up, a South Korean naval officer in working uniform stands with a fully intact, clean and vivid South Korean flag — white field, red-and-blue taeguk circle, four black trigrams — hanging undamaged behind him in the shade, and the low grey silhouette of a warship beyond. Chin lifted, narrowed steady eyes fixed on the approaching column, lips shut in a firm line, jaw set, no hands raised. His face is lit by cold dawn light, not by the fire. no text, no letters, no words, no numbers, no captions, no watermark"
    }
  ]
}
